1. Course content (proprietary)

The course content in this repository and on the published site belongs to
HeyItWorked. It includes the text of every HTML page, the tables and diagrams,
static/css/health-it.css, and everything under static/files/ (lab code,
scripts, sample messages and data).

You may read the content and run the lab code on your own computer for your
own study. You may not copy, republish, adapt, translate, sell, sublicense or
otherwise distribute the course content, in whole or in part, or use it as
training data for machine-learning models, without prior written permission
from the copyright holder. To ask for permission, open an issue at
https://github.com/HeyItWorked/health-it-semester.

GitHub's terms of service let other GitHub users view and fork a public
repository on GitHub. That does not grant any other right in the course
content.

2. Site design (third-party, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0)

The site design is adapted from "The Missing Semester of Your CS Education"
by Anish, Jon and Jose at MIT (https://missing.csail.mit.edu/, source at
https://github.com/missing-semester/missing-semester), licensed under the
Creative Commons Attribution-NonCommercial-ShareAlike 4.0 International
license (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-nc-sa/4.0/). The adapted
parts are:

  - static/css/main.css ("Copyright (c) 2017 Anish Athalye"); changed to load
    the bundled fonts instead of Google Fonts
  - static/css/syntax.css; unchanged
  - static/js/sidenotes.js; changed to place the margin notes again after the
    fonts load
  - the page layout shared by every HTML page: the head, navigation bar,
    content container and footer markup

These adapted parts are licensed under CC BY-NC-SA 4.0, not under section 1.
The original site's analytics were removed.

